2026-11-06T03:00:48.8579427Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8589551Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8590400Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8590845Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8591084Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8591429Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8591818Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8592177Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8592639Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8593090Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8593375Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8594059Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8594445Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8594832Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:00:48.8595548Z   $ sh ./install-nix
